WEBVTT

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.120
Going to see the cherry 
blossoms sounded fishy to me.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.440
They're still only half bloomed!

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.910
<i>Ah... well...
That wasn't the point...</i>

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:28.840
What is then?

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.970
Nobody asked you to do that!

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.100
Besides, the rest of my family
 got to know about it before me.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.150
What's the big idea?!

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.110
<i>You better explain!</i>

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.360
Well, how to say it....

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.940
I'm supposed to keep it 
secret from you but...

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.720
The truth is that today, at your hou-

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.020
Takato!

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.900
Hey! 
I told you to stay hidden!

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.300
<i>Come on, Guilmon!</i>

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.300
Hey, Takato!

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.620
To be honest, I'm uneasy about it.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:58.500
So call it off, okay?

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:15.550
<i>"Wanna be the biggest dreamer?"</i>

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:15.550
<i>Wanna be the biggest dreamer</i>

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:18.200
<i>Running full speed</i>

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:18.200
<i>Zensokuryoku de</i>

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:25.000
<i>through both the future and the present.</i>

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:25.000
<i>Mirai mo ima mo kake nukero</i>

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.000
Ruki-chan?

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:35.840
<i>" The Digimon Runaway Express "</i>

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.400
<i>Oh, right, I've just realized,</i>

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.400
<i>Sou boku wa kizuitan da</i>

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.600
<i>that I always forget to do my homework.</i>

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.600
<i>Zutto shukudai wasureteta</i>

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.500
<i>Here's one unsolvable mystery,</i>

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.500
<i>Sore wa hitotsu no nazo nazo nazo</i>

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.400
<i>"Just who am I?"</i>

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.400
<i>Boku wa dare nan darou</i>

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.800
<i>Even if I happen to slide</i>

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.800
<i>Sliding shite surimuketa hiza</i>

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.600
<i>and skin my knees,</i>

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.600
<i>Itakutatte ne</i>

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.920
<i>I've gotta stand right back up,</i>

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.920
<i>Sugu tachiagaranakya</i>

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:05.260
<i>'cause I know my chance will slip away.</i>

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:05.260
<i>Chance wa nigete yuku wakatteru sa</i>

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.940
<i>Big and bigger, biggest dreamer!</i>

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.940
<i>Big and bigger, biggest dreamer</i>

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:11.600
<i>Dreaming is the start of everything.</i>

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:11.600
<i>Yume miru koto ga subete hajimari</i>

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.300
<i>That's the answer, right?</i>

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.300
<i>Sore ga kotae daro</i>

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:17.160
<i>I'll fly further than anyone,</i>

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:17.160
<i>Dare yori tooku e tonde miseru yo</i>

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.200
<i>through all the tomorrows!</i>

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.200
<i>Subete no asu wo tsuranuite</i>

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.200
<i>"Wanna be the biggest dreamer?"</i>

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.200
<i>Wanna be the biggest dreamer</i>

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:21.820
Here you go.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.200
<i>Running full speed</i>

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.200
<i>Zensokuryoku de</i>

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.500
<i>through both the future and the present.</i>

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.500
<i>Mirai mo ima mo kake nukero</i>

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.150
Hurry up, Guilmon!

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:53.860
Guilmon!

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.560
Guilmon, Evolve!

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.710
Growlmon!

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:30.470
Locomon.

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:31.680
Machine type digimon.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:32.360
Perfect Level.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:33.850
That's not a train...

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.030
It's a Digimon!

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.610
Just what do you think you're doing?

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.320
I must run!

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.800
I must keep running!

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:57.590
What power!

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:04.680
Growlmon!

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.350
Growlmon!

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.400
Takato!

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.220
Go tell Jian and the others!

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.940
Get them to give us a hand!

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.150
Station!

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:27.410
Jian-niichan,
 Yamanote line's this way.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.200
No, we must return directly to Shinjuku.

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:32.600
Eh? We're not going to 
pick Ruki-oneechan up?

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:34.200
Anyway-

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.120
<i>We apologize for the inconvenience.</i>

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:40.100
<i>JR line : Japanese Railway</i>

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:40.100
<i>For the time being, 
the JR line is encountering some issues.</i>

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.130
Hop! What should we do, Jian?

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.680
Let's go back to Ochanomizu and take
 the Marunouchi line to Shinjuku.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.090
I see.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:49.100
The underground, eh?

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.820
We have to walk?

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.780
It looks pretty old...

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.300
I must get to the locomotive.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.630
I have to stop Locomon!

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.420
It still hasn't passed here.

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.440
What's the plan, Ruki?

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.190
I've no idea about that!

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:42.200
I'll think about how to stop 
it once we got onboard!

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.000
Same as always.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.580
Hey, Jian, wait a minute.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:54.460
Ah! I'm hungry! 
I can't walk any further!

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.250
And I'm thirsty...

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.050
All better now, right?

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.710
Huh? Terriermon?

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:05.920
Uh, well....

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:07.150
Lopmon?

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:08.630
My apologies.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.060
What's that?

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.770
Isn't that right above Ichigaya?

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.760
A Digital Zone!

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.980
Is that also because of Locomon?

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.770
If we don't stop it soon...
 Something bad could happen!

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:22.560
Big trouble!

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:32.900
We have a train in Ichigaya that won't stop.

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:33.660
What did you say?

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.600
It'll be dangerous if 
we let it run like that!

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:38.460
No choice. 
We have to stop all the other trains!

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:42.120
Just what's going on?

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:45.000
This is a restricted area!

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:46.180
I'm from the 
Network Administration.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.140
From now on, 
you'll follow my orders.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:54.930
Jian, what is this all about?

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:58.270
The Yamanote and Kanjoh lines run 
into a circle around the city, see?

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.650
Locomon's actions have created 
a distortion in the Network.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:03.780
It looks like that he's waiting 
for something around Ichigaya.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:09.950
And that is for space to erode. We can likely
 expect that a localized distortion will then occur.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:11.690
What should we do then?

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:13.490
This is Yamaki.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:19.000
Computer link completed.
 I will proceed with the scan.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:23.100
Hey, Kenta!

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:26.420
Can't you ditch all this stuff?

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.750
What's wrong, Guilmon?
 Are you all right?

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:37.100
Growlmon did his best but 
Locomon was too strong!

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.200
Where's Takato?

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:40.730
He got on Locomon and left.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.060
He what?!

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:54.080
The brakes should be
around somewhere...

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:05.500
It's here.

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:06.840
Let's go, Renamon!

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:14.400
Takato, what are you doing?

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:15.800
Ruki! Renamon!

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:17.050
We have to hurry up and stop it.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:18.510
I-I know, but...

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.360
I was thinking about using this card, but...

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.520
Guilmon isn't with you?

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.150
We were supposed to
 regroup at Shinjuku...

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:29.190
Not bad. Can I use it?

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:39.320
<i>Card Slash!</i>

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.620
<i>Shellmon Hydro Pressure!</i>

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:47.700
Hot!

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:51.330
The heat is too high. 
This won't be enough.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.040
Sorry.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:55.060
Don't you have something else
 you need to apologize for?

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.920
Eh... ah... that was...

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:03.510
The truth is, Kato-san wanted to have a party, 
and she asked me to call the others...

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:04.680
I get it.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.350
I thought you'd be against it...

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:10.480
That's enough already! For now,
 let's find a way to stop Locomon!

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:12.020
Uh... right.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:17.240
Beelzebumon!

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:18.950
Stand back!

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.130
<i>Wheel Grinder!</i>

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.180
Beelzebumon!

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:46.900
What's that?!

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:48.860
It's coming that way!

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:57.080
Our analysis shows that quantum
 particles are forming at Ichigaya.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:00.660
At this rate, the Digital Zone and the 
Real World will merge together.

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:06.870
If only we could lead it into Ichigaya, we'd be able
 to reverse things by sending it back home.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:10.960
It's mpossible! Even the 
emergency switches aren't working!

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:12.760
Let's do it manually.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:16.760
We build a new track and 
change the route manually.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:17.800
It's the only way.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:20.600
But where do we do that?

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.520
If possible, then...

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:23.930
Yoyogi Station!

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:29.820
Hey!

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:34.050
You guys! We have to stop 
that Digimon somehow!

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:35.650
Takato is already on it.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:37.030
Really, Guilmon?

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:40.580
Yup. Locomon was a lot 
stronger than Growlmon.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:42.150
Let's go after it!

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:45.820
And how do we do that?
 Locomon is too fast for us to catch up to him.

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:47.120
We'll use that.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.960
With Guardromon's power,
 we should be able to move it.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:52.450
Just leave it to me!

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:58.590
And Terriermon?

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:02.060
To be honest... 
I mixed them up...

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:08.500
Geez! That was rude, Jian!

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:10.860
There, there, Terriermon.

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:25.030
What did you say?! We have a problem!
 There are children on that Digimon!

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:26.400
That's not possible!

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:29.280
A station attendant saw them,
 there's no doubt about it!

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:31.330
Children?

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:42.860
Yamaki-san!

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:44.180
<i>I thought it'd be you guys.</i>

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:45.300
Listen carefully.

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:48.680
We're trying to lead this Digimon
 towards the Soubu line.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:52.650
And for that, we have to change 
its route at the Yoyogi Station.

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:54.640
<i>You must get off it immediately.</i>

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.800
Alright, got it!

00:11:57.700 --> 00:11:59.450
We can leave the rest to Yamaki-san!

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:01.620
"Got it", my ass!

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:04.320
But without Guilmon...

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:06.610
So you can't do anything by yourself?

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:14.090
I don't trust adults...

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.460
Here we go!
 We'll leave it to you, Guardromon!

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.730
I'll stop this train myself!

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:40.070
Hurry up!
 Speed up, Guardromon!

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:41.790
Got it!

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:53.330
We have little time left until 
they reach Yoyogi Station.

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:56.920
Takato-kun,
 you guys need to get off now!

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.350
We can still make it!

00:12:58.540 --> 00:12:59.900
<i>Stop it! 
Don't do anything dangerous!</i>

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:03.000
If something happens, 
we can detach the cars.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:03.770
Later.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:11.300
Let's keep trying a bit more. 
Besides, there's no way to get off at this speed.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:14.680
Ruki.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:20.980
Yamaki-san said there's a 
Digital Zone at Ichigaya and...

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:31.700
We'll be together forever and ever, 
as we promised under the setting sun.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:41.760
I want to see you soon, hoping that 
these feelings of mine will reach you.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:42.660
Dad!

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:50.730
I hate singing.

00:13:52.340 --> 00:14:01.560
As you unexpectedly dove
 into my lonely heart,

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:11.660
you gently wrapped up 
the pieces that sting a bit.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:20.840
It was the first time I felt so relieved

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:30.400
so I squeezed that warmth 
into my outside pocket.

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:35.060
I feel like taking a walk.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:39.970
<i>We'll be together forever and ever,</i>

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:45.650
<i>as we promised under the setting sun.</i>

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:49.480
<i>When you feel lonely,</i>

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:54.370
<i>take a look at the orange horizon,</i>

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:59.160
<i>and the setting sun will whisper to you,</i>

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:04.620
<i>"it will all be fine".</i>

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:08.750
<i>I want to see you soon,</i>

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:14.560
<i>hoping that these feelings 
of mine will reach you...</i>

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:17.090
Ruki?

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:20.480
Ruki, what's wrong?

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:25.270
Ruki?! 
What are you doing?!

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:27.310
You're wrong.

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:32.290
Don't get in my way.
 I want to sing...

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:33.040
Ruki?

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:39.750
It's here.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:44.750
Got it!

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:52.500
Do you copy?
 It just passed through Yoyogi.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:54.930
Huh?! 
There's another train following it!

00:15:58.190 --> 00:15:59.800
Farewell!

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:04.670
Ah! It's here!

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:06.480
Yay~ Yay~

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:08.100
It's dangerous, Xiaochun!

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:14.240
Ruki-oneechan?

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.360
That can't be.

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:19.160
Takato-niichan and Renamon were there too!

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:24.050
Eh?! Waah!
 Big trouble! Big trouble!

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:26.500
Here you go, Lopmon!

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:27.540
Understood.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:31.680
Terriermon!

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:33.100
You're late!

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.050
Welcome back, Lopmon!

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:39.980
We've caught up!

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:47.900
Hey Guilmon!

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:49.190
We're going ahead!

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:51.360
Guys!

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:54.190
I have to hurry and find Takato.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:58.870
Takato!

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:01.370
Is he gonna be fine?

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.670
I've gotta wonder, about Guilmon...

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:05.700
How did he get on it anyway?

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:12.050
Renamon?

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:12.640
What's going on?

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:15.090
Ruki is...

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:19.010
Stop it, Ruki!

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:22.140
Ruki!

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:32.100
Crap!

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:44.940
Hey, Takato-kun!
 What's going on?!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.590
Ruki, what are you doing?!

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:53.830
Don't get in my way. 
I want to sing.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:58.220
If we don't do anything, Locomon will 
take us with him to the Digital Zone-

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:00.470
Takato, found you!

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:01.130
Guilmon!

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:06.610
Just what are those two doing?!

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:09.500
That smell...

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.680
Hey, Guilmon! Guilmon!

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:13.440
<i>Fireball!</i>

00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:16.190
That's not gonna help us!

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:16.910
Ruki!

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:31.540
Ruki!

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:34.720
Parasite Digimon, Parasimon.

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:36.290
But how?!

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.600
Look over there!

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:42.310
Locomon is being controlled by a Parasimon!

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.770
I must keep running!

00:18:45.510 --> 00:18:46.650
Let go of Ruki!

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:52.100
I... want to sing...

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:54.480
It just passed Shinagawa Station.

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:56.570
The Yoyogi line is almost done!

00:18:58.270 --> 00:18:59.790
Yamaki-san? 
We're out of time!

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.990
Now, we can only wait.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:04.040
<i>I believe in those kids.</i>

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:07.370
Snap out of it, Ruki!

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:15.930
Takato!

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:22.350
Stop it, Ruki!

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:24.220
Clear the way!

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:26.620
Yoyogi, standby, OK.

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:31.810
Locomon is almost in position.

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:37.930
<i>Rock Breaker!</i>

00:19:41.230 --> 00:19:41.820
Takato!

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:45.210
Now! Change the route!

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:46.820
Changing the route!

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:55.500
Thanks, Guilmon.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:56.580
Ruki!

00:19:59.170 --> 00:19:59.880
Ruki!

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:02.590
Ruki!

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:07.140
Takato!

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:18.720
Locomon change!

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:21.980
GrandLocomon!

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:24.700
Ah! He transformed!

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:26.140
No, he evolved!

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:28.580
GrandLocomon. 
Ultimate level.

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:30.000
It's true!

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:35.000
If we don't do anything, 
we'll all get caught into the Digital Zone!

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:43.920
Let me go!
 Otherwise, we'll both fall!

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:47.930
You idiot! Giving up that 
easily isn't like you at all!

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:52.010
What happened to the Ruki I know? 
Don't give up, Ruki!

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:57.140
Come on, Guardromon!

00:20:57.310 --> 00:20:57.650
Right!

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:04.360
Ruki!

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:04.990
Renamon!

00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:06.870
Hurry up, Renamon!

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:18.330
He's trying to cut us off!

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:19.500
Wait, Ruki!

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:21.540
Let's go, Guilmon!

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:27.300
Ruki!

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:30.430
Help me! Takato!

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:31.270
Ruki!

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:37.190
Let's go! Guilmon!

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:44.100
<i>Matrix Evolution!</i>

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:53.410
Guilmon, Evolve!

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:11.350
Dukemon!

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:18.340
Let go of Ruki!

00:22:19.180 --> 00:22:20.480
Takato!

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:22.180
You naive twat!

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:32.110
Renamon!

00:22:33.070 --> 00:22:34.900
It was all the Parasimon's doing.

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:37.840
They took control of
 both you and Locomon.

00:22:38.200 --> 00:22:40.630
But thanks to them, 
we got to hear this beautiful song.

00:22:45.750 --> 00:22:49.470
For letting us hear Ruki's song,
 have a taste... of my thanks!

00:22:52.400 --> 00:22:54.900
<i>Royal Saber!</i>

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:08.990
My job is done! GrandLocomon, 
you will keep running forever!

00:23:11.690 --> 00:23:12.750
The Digital Zone is-

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:16.630
We have a problem! 
Wild Ones are Realizing!

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:17.370
What did you say?!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:20.830
What's that over there, Lopmon?

00:23:23.580 --> 00:23:24.130
Could it be...

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:28.710
Jian, big trouble!

00:23:28.710 --> 00:23:31.300
A lot of them are coming
 from the Digital Zone!

00:23:35.480 --> 00:23:38.430
I understand...
this was their objective!

00:23:38.800 --> 00:23:39.520
Objective?

00:23:39.970 --> 00:23:43.230
They had Locomon run wild 
to open the Digital Zone.

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:45.690
And from there, the Parasimon 
will be able to Realize.

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:49.230
In short, they came to the
 Real World... to invade it!

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:50.820
We won't let it happen!

00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:55.250
<i>Matrix Evolution!</i>

00:23:59.330 --> 00:24:00.490
Terriermon, Evolve!

00:24:05.080 --> 00:24:06.370
Renamon, Evolve!

00:24:19.050 --> 00:24:20.550
SaintGalgomon!

00:24:24.350 --> 00:24:25.820
Sakuyamon!

00:24:26.810 --> 00:24:29.310
Let's stop them at the entrance
 of the Digital Zone!

00:24:42.620 --> 00:24:44.130
<i>Burst Shot!</i>

00:25:06.890 --> 00:25:07.500
They just keep coming!

00:25:08.640 --> 00:25:10.560
What is this?! 
It's different from the others!

00:25:11.190 --> 00:25:12.060
It's going to Realize!

00:25:17.740 --> 00:25:18.360
It's coming!

00:25:24.400 --> 00:25:25.420
Sup, guys!

00:25:25.420 --> 00:25:26.410
Justimon!

00:25:26.920 --> 00:25:27.910
Ryo-san?

00:25:36.670 --> 00:25:37.760
Ouch!

00:25:37.760 --> 00:25:39.260
<i>Beam!</i>

00:25:52.730 --> 00:25:54.130
Beelzebumon!

00:25:54.520 --> 00:25:57.740
<i>Accel Arm!</i>

00:26:00.990 --> 00:26:01.950
There's too many of them!

00:26:02.160 --> 00:26:03.070
We won't make it!

00:26:12.340 --> 00:26:13.130
Dukemon!

00:26:16.210 --> 00:26:17.800
We can't afford to lose...

00:26:18.800 --> 00:26:23.260
We can't let... 
the Parasimon do as they please!

00:26:35.480 --> 00:26:36.110
So pretty...

00:26:38.230 --> 00:26:41.070
Dukemon, Crimson Mode!

00:26:45.420 --> 00:26:46.420
<i>Quo Vadis!</i>

00:27:08.640 --> 00:27:09.350
Locomon?

00:27:09.360 --> 00:27:12.500
I must run.
 I must keep running!

00:27:20.150 --> 00:27:21.410
What's with this guy?

00:27:21.650 --> 00:27:24.710
He's no different than when he 
was controlled by Parasimon!

00:27:27.800 --> 00:27:29.240
Happy Birthday!

00:27:39.140 --> 00:27:40.680
Go on, blow out the candles!

00:27:46.750 --> 00:27:52.820
I've gotta stand right back up, 
'cause I know my chance will slip away!

00:27:53.250 --> 00:27:59.510
I'm telling you, Tamers gather a collection of 
cards for the sake of justice! You hear? And so-

00:28:06.110 --> 00:28:07.340
Next is Ruki-oneechan!

00:28:07.570 --> 00:28:09.070
Eh?! Ruki?!

00:28:09.070 --> 00:28:11.790
Sing us something!
 I heard that you were great at it!

00:28:11.790 --> 00:28:13.700
Stop! You can't just ask like that!

00:28:18.540 --> 00:28:20.550
Ah, she got mad.

00:28:20.550 --> 00:28:21.790
Then, I'll take her place!

00:28:22.670 --> 00:28:24.600
What's wrong with Ruki ~culu?

00:28:28.950 --> 00:28:35.790
C'mon, start running now,
 to a place that's not on maps!

00:28:40.610 --> 00:28:41.440
Ruki.

00:28:54.650 --> 00:28:58.420
<i>Zutto zutto issho ni iru to</i>

00:28:54.650 --> 00:28:58.420
<i>We'll be together forever and ever,</i>

00:28:58.420 --> 00:29:03.300
<i>Ano yuuhi ni yakusoku shita kara</i>

00:28:58.420 --> 00:29:03.300
<i>as we promised under the setting sun.</i>

00:29:03.300 --> 00:29:06.420
<i>Ima sugu aitai</i>

00:29:03.300 --> 00:29:06.420
<i>I want to see you soon,</i>

00:29:06.420 --> 00:29:13.200
<i>Sono kimochi wo onegai tsutaete ne</i>

00:29:06.420 --> 00:29:13.200
<i>hoping that these feelings of mine will reach you.</i>

00:29:20.200 --> 00:29:23.700
<i>Hitoribotchi no kokoro ni</i>

00:29:20.200 --> 00:29:23.700
<i>As you unexpectedly</i>

00:29:23.700 --> 00:29:27.660
<i>Totsuzen tobikonde kita</i>

00:29:23.700 --> 00:29:27.660
<i>dove into my lonely heart,</i>

00:29:27.660 --> 00:29:31.650
<i>Sukoshi itakatta koto</i>

00:29:27.660 --> 00:29:31.650
<i>you gently wrapped up</i>

00:29:31.650 --> 00:29:36.160
<i>Yasashiku tsutsunde kureta</i>

00:29:31.650 --> 00:29:36.160
<i>the pieces that sting a bit.</i>

00:29:36.160 --> 00:29:40.850
<i>Konna ni hotto suru koto wa</i>

00:29:36.160 --> 00:29:40.850
<i>It was the first time</i>

00:29:40.850 --> 00:29:43.680
<i>Hajimete dakara</i>

00:29:40.850 --> 00:29:43.680
<i>I felt so relieved</i>

00:29:43.680 --> 00:29:47.600
<i>Sono nukumori wo sotto</i>

00:29:43.680 --> 00:29:47.600
<i>so I squeezed that warmth</i>

00:29:47.600 --> 00:29:51.700
<i>Pocket ni tsume konde</i>

00:29:47.600 --> 00:29:51.700
<i>into my outside pocket.</i>

00:29:51.700 --> 00:29:55.680
<i>Aruite ikitai</i>

00:29:51.700 --> 00:29:55.680
<i>I feel like taking a walk.</i>

00:29:55.680 --> 00:29:59.500
<i>Zutto zutto issho ni iru to</i>

00:29:55.680 --> 00:29:59.500
<i>We'll be together forever and ever,</i>

00:29:59.500 --> 00:30:04.200
<i>Ano yuuhi ni yakusoku shita kara</i>

00:29:59.500 --> 00:30:04.200
<i>as we promised under the setting sun.</i>

00:30:04.200 --> 00:30:07.550
<i>Ima sugu aitai</i>

00:30:04.200 --> 00:30:07.550
<i>I want to see you soon,</i>

00:30:07.550 --> 00:30:14.500
<i>Sono kimochi wo onegai tsutaete ne</i>

00:30:07.550 --> 00:30:14.500
<i>hoping that these feelings of mine will reach you.</i>

00:30:14.500 --> 00:30:16.500
<i></i>

00:30:16.500 --> 00:30:18.500
<i></i>

